#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose the CPU, memory, and GPU resources for a managed workflow, and define"
" sizes that match the size of the problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a compute profile {#choose-a-compute-profile}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Managed workflows run on compute profiles. A compute profile is a fixed "
"combination of vCPUs, memory, and GPUs, similar to the resources that you "
"request from an HPC scheduler. When you upload a workflow, you map its "
"sizes, such as `S` and `M`, to profiles, and each run picks one of those "
"sizes. The job then runs on its own node with that profile, and keeps the "
"profile until the job ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Profile | vCPUs | Memory (GB) | GPUs |\n"
"| - | - | - | - |\n"
"| `8x32` | 8 | 32 | None |\n"
"| `16x128` | 16 | 128 | None |\n"
"| `48x768` | 48 | 768 | None |\n"
"| `128x1500` | 128 | 1500 | None |\n"
"| `24x120x1l40s` | 24 | 120 | 1 L40S |\n"
"| `20x320x2a100` | 20 | 320 | 2 A100 |\n"
"| `80x1200x8a100` | 80 | 1200 | 8 A100 |\n"
"| `160x1792x8h100` | 160 | 1792 | 8 H100 |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A profile ID has the form `{cpu}x{memory}`, with memory in GB, or "
"`{cpu}x{memory}x{count}{gpu}` for a profile with GPUs. For example, "
"`24x120x1l40s` has 24 vCPUs, 120 GB of memory, and one NVIDIA L40S GPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check available profiles {#check-available-profiles}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To see which profiles are available, call `compute_profiles()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Look up a profile by its resources {#look-up-a-profile-by-its-resources}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead of typing a profile ID, you can describe the resources that your "
"workflow needs with `compute_profile()`, and use the result as a value in "
"`sizes_map`. Pass `cpu` and `memory` in GB, and pass `gpu` for a GPU "
"profile:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A `sizes_map` accepts profile IDs and the profiles that `compute_profile()` "
"returns, and you can mix both in one map. To check a profile ID before you "
"upload, pass it to `compute_profile()`, for example "
"`client.compute_profile(\"16x128\")`. If no profile matches, the error lists"
" the available profiles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`compute_profiles()` returns a list, so you can also filter it yourself. For"
" example, the following code finds the GPU profiles:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set a default compute profile for your workflow {#set-a-default-compute-"
"profile-for-your-workflow}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most workflows start with one size. Map it to a profile with `sizes_map`, "
"and make it the default with `default_size`, when you upload the workflow:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every run of the workflow uses this profile, so you do not need to pass a "
"size when you run it:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Best practice: match sizes to problem sizes {#best-practice-match-sizes-to-"
"problem-sizes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A workflow solves specific problems, and it might require different compute "
"profiles as the problems increase in scale and complexity. With a "
"`sizes_map` for each workflow, you can do the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Give large problems enough compute resources to run to completion.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prevent small problems from using a larger node than they need.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can base the sizes on the factors that determine your workflow's memory "
"and CPU use, such as the subspace size, the number of batches, or the number"
" of qubits.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define the sizes {#define-the-sizes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can map up to four sizes, for small (`S`), medium (`M`), large (`L`), "
"and extra-large (`XL`) problems. For example, the following code defines a "
"workflow with three sizes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Size rules {#size-rules}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Size labels must be `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`, so a workflow can define up to "
"four sizes. A managed workflow matches labels in uppercase or lowercase, and"
" stores them in uppercase. Two sizes can map to the same profile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A workflow rejects the first upload in the following cases:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A label is not `S`, `M`, `L`, or `XL`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You set `sizes_map` without `default_size`, or `default_size` without "
"`sizes_map`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`default_size` is not one of the labels in `sizes_map`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A value in `sizes_map` is not an available compute profile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change sizes on re-upload {#change-sizes-on-re-upload}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you upload the workflow again with the same `title`, the managed "
"workflow handles the sizes as follows:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If you set `sizes_map`, the new sizes replace all of the stored sizes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you omit `sizes_map`, the workflow keeps the stored sizes and the "
"default.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To change only the default, set `default_size` without `sizes_map`. The "
"value of `default_size` must be one of the stored sizes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set `default_size` every time that you set `sizes_map`. A re-upload does not"
" require `default_size`. If the new sizes do not include the old default, "
"the workflow has no default, and every run without `function_size` fails.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a size for each run {#choose-a-size-for-each-run}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pass `function_size` to `run()` to choose one of the workflow's sizes for "
"that job. If you omit it, the job uses the workflow's default size:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`sizes()` and `get_default_size()` return the sizes that were stored when "
"you loaded the workflow. To see sizes that changed after you loaded the "
"workflow, load it again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To read the size and compute profile of the job, call `get_function_size()` "
"and `get_compute_profile()` in your workflow code:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot sizes {#troubleshoot-sizes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| The upload fails with `Invalid size '...'. Valid sizes are: S, M, L, XL.` | A label in `sizes_map` is not one of the four supported labels. |\n"
"| The upload fails with `Unknown compute profile '...' for size '...'.` | A value in `sizes_map` is not an available profile. Check the ID with `compute_profiles()`, or use `compute_profile()` to look it up. |\n"
"| `compute_profile()` fails with `No compute profile matches ...` | No profile has exactly those resources. For a GPU profile, also pass `gpu`. Pick a profile from the list in the error. |\n"
"| The upload fails with `'default_size' is required when 'sizes' is provided.` | The first upload sets `sizes_map` without `default_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Unknown function size '...' for this function. Available sizes: ...` | The workflow does not define the size that you passed to `function_size`. |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `This function has no size.` | A re-upload replaced the sizes and removed the default. Upload again with `default_size`, or pass `function_size`. |\n"
msgstr ""
